  "home": {
    "alerts": {
      "innerHTML": "\n    <div class=\"alert\" data-lvl=\"1\" role=\"alert\">\n      <strong>Flood Watch</strong>\n      <p>Flood Watch issued April 14 at 5:12AM EDT until April 16 at 8:00AM EDT by NWS Albany NY</p>\n      <details><summary>Details</summary><pre>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall and snowmelt is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southern Vermont, including Windham County.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers, creeks and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\nYou should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood Warnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared to take action should flooding develop.</pre></details>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"alert\" data-lvl=\"2\" role=\"alert\">\n      <strong>Wind Advisory</strong>\n      <p>Wind Advisory issued April 14 at 5:12AM EDT until April 16 at 6:00PM EDT by NWS Albany NY</p>\n      <details><summary>Details</summary><pre>* WHAT...West winds 15 to 25 mph with gusts up to 40 mph expected.\n\n* WHERE...Windham County.\n\nWinds this strong can blow around unsecured objects. Boats on open water should secure moorings.</pre></details>\n    </div>",
